ht because there's big  investments to make platforms in United  Kingdom factories but over a period of  time as they sure as the car companies  change over to the new cars those cars  will not come to the United Kingdom it's  nothing to do with fear it's everything  to do with reality brexit is the most  immediate worry but the car industry is  planning for a future shaped by many  other challenges there's some real real  concerns across all manufacturers but  it's one to be honest with you amongst  many I mean electrification co2 is also  big concern for manufacturers as well as  how do we meet those and at the same  time how do we make electric vehicles  accessible to many but electric cars  will take decades to perfect brexit is  imminent and its effects on this  industry are now resonating Adam Parsons  Sky News Geneva
 

